--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -72,6 +72,13 @@ counts when the permission is checked on that project. Nobody can hand out, take
 a role that carries a permission they do not hold themselves, so an admin cannot make anyone an
 owner or demote one.
 
+`POST /v1/orgs/{org_id}/role-assignments:bulk` takes `{"items": [{user_id, role_id,
+project_id?}, …]}` (1–100 items) and applies each item on its own: one that fails (unknown
+member, role or project, a role the caller cannot hand out, an existing assignment) does not stop
+the others. The answer is 200 with one result per item, in the order of the request:
+`{"status": "created", "user_id", "assignment_id"}` or `{"status": "failed", "user_id",
+"error": {code, message, details?}}`. Each created assignment writes its own audit event.
+
 All decisions go through `AuthorizationService.check(principal, permission, resource)`; routes
 declare what they need with the `require(permission, resource_from=…)` dependency.
 
